🧠 Introduction

Embeddings are one of the most important concepts in:

* RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)
* Semantic Search
* Recommendation Systems
* Document Similarity
* Clustering

👉 They convert text into numerical vectors that capture meaning.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is an Embedding?

```text id="embedding_def"
A dense numerical vector representation of text that captures semantic meaning
```

---

📌 Example

Text:

```text id="embed_example"
"Artificial Intelligence is transforming the world."
```

Embedding (simplified):

```text id="embed_vector"
[0.12, -0.87, 0.45, ...]
```

---

🧠 Why Embeddings are Important

Words and sentences with similar meanings produce similar vectors.

### Example

* "What is AI?"
* "Explain Artificial Intelligence"

👉 Their embeddings will be very close.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📐 Embedding Dimensions

Typical vector sizes:

* 384 dimensions
* 768 dimensions
* 1024 dimensions
* 1536 dimensions
* 3072 dimensions

More dimensions can capture richer information, but require more storage and compute.

---

🔍 Similarity Search

Embeddings are compared using:

* Cosine Similarity
* Dot Product
* Euclidean Distance

---

📌 Cosine Similarity

```text id="cosine_similarity"
Measures how similar two vectors are (range: -1 to 1)
```

Higher similarity → more semantically related.

